# Line endings. This project is edited on both a Mac and a Windows PC, and
# without this every file looks fully rewritten after a round trip because one
# machine writes CRLF and the other LF — which buries real changes in noise and
# causes phantom merge conflicts.
#
# Normalise to LF in the repository; Git checks out whatever each OS prefers.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch these, and never try to diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.onnx binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Minified vendor libraries are not worth diffing either — collapse them in
# pull requests so a real change is not lost in a 1 MB single-line file.
*.min.js linguist-vendored -diff
